### Switch Markdown syntax highlighting to Prism with markdown.syntaxHighlight

Source: https://github.com/withastro/docs/blob/main/src/content/docs/en/reference/configuration-reference.mdx

Set markdown.syntaxHighlight to 'prism' in astro.config.mjs to use Prism instead of the default Shiki highlighter. You must provide your own Prism stylesheet.

```javascript
// astro.config.mjs
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';

export default defineConfig({
  markdown: {
    // Example: Switch to use prism for syntax highlighting in Markdown
    syntaxHighlight: 'prism',
  }
});
```

--------------------------------

### Configure satteri Markdown processor plugins in astro.config.mjs

Source: https://github.com/withastro/docs/blob/main/src/content/docs/en/guides/markdown-content.mdx

Pass options directly as an options object to plugin functions when configuring mdast or hast plugins in the satteri processor.

```javascript
import { defineConfig } from "astro/config";
import { satteri } from "@astrojs/markdown-satteri";
import imgAttr from "satteri-imgattr";
import satteriCallouts from "satteri-callouts";

export default defineConfig({
  markdown: {
    processor: satteri({
      mdastPlugins: [
        imgAttr({
          defaults: { loading: "lazy", decoding: "async" },
        }),
      ],
      hastPlugins: [satteriCallouts()],
    }),
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### satteri()

Source: https://github.com/withastro/docs/blob/main/src/content/docs/en/reference/markdown-processors/satteri.mdx

Creates a Sätteri-based Markdown processor to render `.md` and `.mdx` files. Pass it to `markdown.processor` to customize the Markdown rendering behavior.

```APIDOC
## satteri()

### Description
Creates a Sätteri-based Markdown processor to render `.md` and `.mdx` files. Pass it to `markdown.processor` to customize the Markdown rendering behavior.

### Signature
`(options?: SatteriProcessorOptions) => MarkdownProcessor`

### Parameters
- **options** (SatteriProcessorOptions) - Optional - Configuration options for the Sätteri processor.

#### Options
- **options.mdastPlugins** (MdastPluginList | undefined) - Optional - Default: `[]`. Pass Sätteri mdast plugins to customize how your Markdown is built.
- **options.hastPlugins** (HastPluginList | undefined) - Optional - Default: `[]`. Pass Sätteri hast plugins to customize how your HTML is generated from the Markdown content.
- **options.features** (SatteriFeatures) - Optional - Default: `{}`. Customize the features available in Sätteri.
  - **options.features.smartPunctuation** (boolean | object) - Optional - Default: `true`. Whether to use smart punctuation to convert straight quotes to curly quotes, double hyphens to em dashes, and three dots to ellipses. You can either disable it or provide a configuration object with the properties supported by Sätteri to customize its behavior.

### Example
```js title="astro.config.mjs"
import { satteri } from "@astrojs/markdown-satteri";
import { satteriEmoji } from "satteri-emoji";

export default {
  markdown: {
    processor: satteri({
      mdastPlugins: [satteriEmoji],
    }),
  },
};
```
```

--------------------------------

### Configure unified Markdown processor with markdown.processor

Source: https://github.com/withastro/docs/blob/main/src/content/docs/en/reference/configuration-reference.mdx

To keep the remark/rehype pipeline, install @astrojs/markdown-remark and pass unified() to markdown.processor.

```js
// astro.config.mjs
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';
import { unified } from '@astrojs/markdown-remark';
import remarkToc from 'remark-toc';

export default defineConfig({
  markdown: {
    processor: unified({
      remarkPlugins: [remarkToc],
    }),
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### Unified API Reference > Imports from `@astrojs/markdown-remark` > `unified()`

Source: https://github.com/withastro/docs/blob/main/src/content/docs/en/reference/markdown-processors/unified.mdx

**Type:** <code>(options?: <a href="#options">UnifiedProcessorOptions</a>) => <a href="#markdownprocessor">MarkdownProcessor</a></code><br />
<Since v="7.2.0" pkg="@astrojs/markdown-remark" />

Creates a unified-based processor to render `.md` and `.mdx` files. Pass it to [`markdown.processor`](/en/reference/configuration-reference/#markdownprocessor) to use unified as the default Markdown processor.

<ReadMore>Learn more about [setting up a Markdown processor](/en/guides/markdown-content/#setting-up-a-markdown-processor) and [using remark and rehype plugins](/en/guides/markdown-content/#markdown-processor-plugins) with examples.</ReadMore>

